HUAKAI vendors the Cloudflare boring Rust crates inside the MIT-licensed
core_gateway exploratory workspace.

Upstream source:
- Repository: https://github.com/cloudflare/boring
- Locked release package: boring-5.1.0 / boring-sys-5.1.0
- VCS commit recorded by the crates.io package:
  3acc9820eb7117f0b36078bf119c81c5ea337e6a
- Local reference note: /home/codex/refs/boring was at
  3921f35aa406c4cbff6efca9688f1fc9ead2508f and had no local tag refs; its
  BoringSSL submodule directory was empty. To preserve the complete release
  tree, this vendor copy uses the local crates.io cache for boring 5.1.0.

Vendored material:
- boring/      : Rust bindings for BoringSSL, licensed Apache-2.0.
- boring-sys/  : low-level BoringSSL FFI crate, licensed MIT for the Rust crate
  material. Its deps/boringssl subtree keeps the BoringSSL license file shipped
  in the boring-sys 5.1.0 package.
- LICENSE      : Apache-2.0 license text copied from upstream boring/LICENSE.

Reason for this local vendor copy:
HUAKAI needs byte-level ClientHello control for the R-2-B/R-3-A mimicry path.
The upstream boring 5.1.0 API can build the TLS connector used by HUAKAI, but
its default ClientHello extension ordering does not match the observed
CodexCli, KiroCli, or GeminiAdvanced samples. The planned HUAKAI fork will add
a narrow SslContextBuilder surface for caller-specified extension ordering.

